WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.139
Public key infrastructure is the trust framework that makes web service authentication scale.

2
00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:23.419
Server certificates, certificate authorities, intermediate chains, trust stores, revocation mechanisms, certificate transparency practices, and browser or operating system policies all contribute to the decision a client makes when it accepts a TLS connection.

3
00:00:23.419 --> 00:00:29.785
For a web service, the certificate is not just a file on disk; it is part of a larger ecosystem of trust.

4
00:00:29.785 --> 00:00:33.044
Digital signatures are central to that ecosystem.

5
00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:41.077
Certificates are signed, certificate chains are verified, and clients must understand the signature algorithms involved.

6
00:00:41.077 --> 00:00:55.098
Post-quantum signature algorithms can introduce larger signatures or certificates, and that may affect handshake size, network behavior, memory usage, embedded clients, legacy devices, middleboxes, and logging.

7
00:00:55.098 --> 00:01:02.450
The concern is not only whether an algorithm is strong; it is whether the surrounding ecosystem can use it reliably.

8
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.557
Certificate migration depends on many parties.

9
00:01:05.557 --> 00:01:21.018
Browsers, operating systems, certificate authorities, TLS libraries, hardware security modules, cloud platforms, device vendors, enterprise trust stores, mobile platforms, and security inspection products all influence readiness.

10
00:01:21.018 --> 00:01:32.538
A service owner may be eager to move, but if clients cannot validate the chain or a managed platform does not support the needed options, production migration may be blocked or risky.

11
00:01:32.538 --> 00:01:35.342
It also helps to separate related use cases.

12
00:01:35.342 --> 00:01:47.771
Code signing, service identity, device identity, and web server certificates all use digital signatures, but they have different validation paths, lifetimes, and operational consequences.

13
00:01:47.771 --> 00:01:53.683
Teams should track ecosystem readiness before changing production certificate strategy.

14
00:01:53.683 --> 00:02:05.506
The near-term planning move is to inventory certificate use, understand dependencies, follow reputable guidance, and avoid one-off certificate choices that clients cannot handle.
